id: pm-slack-standup-xms9
title: "Adopt the pm-cli 2026.7.26 typed authoring SDK, drop the last any-typed shim, and de-binary the source file"
description: "This package was missed by the fleet-wide 2026.7.26 typed-authoring rollout and was the 14th and last package still carrying the retired any-typed defineExtension shim. Replace it with the fleet-standard locally declared typed identity helper constrained by the SDK's own ExtensionModule, bump the host to 2026.7.26, and declare the peer dependency the rest of the fleet declares. Also replaces a literal NUL byte in the source with its escape sequence."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-26T21:24:56.653Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T21:25:22.551Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-26T21:25:22.550Z"
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: No any remains in the source; the extension activates and every command runs against a real workspace; index.ts is plain UTF-8 text and greppable; peerDependencies matches the fleet convention.
resolution: Shim replaced with the typed identity helper; host bumped to 2026.7.26 with the fleet-standard peer dependency declared; literal NUL replaced with its escape sequence.
actual_result: "Zero any in the source. 91/91 unit tests green and typecheck clean under real SDK types. Functionally verified in a throwaway workspace, not just under unit tests: pm install activated the extension with 0 activation failures and 3 registered actions; pm standup correctly refused to post with no webhook (exit 2, actionable message); --dry-run categorised 4 real items as 2 in-progress / 0 blocked / 1 up-next; after adding a real blocked_by edge it correctly re-categorised to 1 in-progress / 1 blocked and rendered the blocker id; standup export --format json emitted a valid Block Kit payload. index.ts now reports as UTF-8 text and grep finds symbols in it."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T21:25:11.865Z",codex,"THE any SHIM. This package carried the shim the pt2 rollout removed from 13 others:\n\n    const defineExtension: typeof defineExtensionType = ((extension: any) => extension) as any;\n\nTwo any casts, and its justification comment asserted that 'standalone-installed extensions load only their own dist/, so @unbrained/pm-cli is not resolvable at runtime'. That premise is FALSE and was corrected upstream in pm-cli#717 — the SDK is importable at runtime wherever the package's own node_modules is populated.\n\nReplaced with the fleet-standard helper, constrained by the SDK's own type so the extension object is contract-checked exactly as the imported helper would check it:\n\n    const defineExtension = <TModule extends ExtensionModule>(module: TModule): TModule => module;\n\nKept type-only deliberately (import type from @unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/authoring). Reason is availability, not impossibility: a standalone-installed extension is not GUARANTEED a populated node_modules, so a value import would make activation depend on it. The EXIT_CODE comment was reworded to say that accurately instead of overclaiming.\n\nNote the sdk/authoring subpath does not exist in 2026.7.25, which this package was pinned to — the host bump was a prerequisite, not a nicety.\n\nTHE NUL BYTE. index.ts contained a literal 0x00 character at line 1310, inside a composite dedupe key:\n\n    const dedupeKey = `${target.webhookUrl}<NUL>${target.channel ?? \"\"}`;\n\nThe technique is sound — a NUL separator cannot collide with anything inside a URL or channel name, so it prevents ('ab','c') and ('a','bc') hashing alike. But writing it as a RAW BYTE rather than the \\\\u0000 escape made the whole 2104-line file binary: 'file' reported 'data', and grep -I (the default in most agent tooling, including Claude Code's wrapper) SILENTLY SKIPPED THE ENTIRE FILE. An agent searching this package for any symbol got zero hits and would reasonably conclude the code did not exist. For a project whose thesis is 'project management = context management', a source file invisible to search is a real defect. Replaced with the escape sequence: byte-identical at runtime, file is now plain UTF-8."
close_reason: completed
body: ""
